Z||000002||Coconut||07-09-2000||10:32 AM||||How's it going Rick?,<P>Welcome to the #1 place on the net for anything that has to do with our beloved Fieros. You will find your visits here to be informative and enjoyable. It's really great to meet new members and see what kinda stuff they are into. There are all kinds of different folks here from Doctors to Railroad Switchmen to Students to Truck Drivers to Secretaries and we all have a common LOVE for that little plastic car sitting out in the driveway. Enjoy your stay, You'll love it here! Post a few pics if you can. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Cruisin' On,<BR>Coconut <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut_2.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||GT Bastard||07-09-2000||02:37 PM||||I replaced my tranny cooler lines before... Just go to the auto parts store and ask for tranny fluid line.  Couple bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||07-09-2000||02:42 PM||||Welcome to the Forum 'Blue" -- when looking for parts, you might also check with George out at The Fiero Shop in Hayward, CA  <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroshop.net</A>  -- he has several parts cars and his parts prices are below anyone else I have found, even with shipping. He ships anywhere in the IS via UPS (there ya go Gokart!!) and usually has what you need. George not only supplies parts but repairs and restores Fieros as well so he really knows what he is doing. (Funny thing, he just sold an '87 Blue GT right before I left there two weeks ago - I thought for a minute this was it.......) -- anyway, check with him either for parts or mechanical how-to.......and again, welcome to the forum......<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/my_fiero_sig.gif">   <BR>'87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
